>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `ASTAR_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.ASTAR_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by A-star classical search.

`ASTAR_TAC thms` safely saturates the whole state, then expands the first
open goal using the fast instantiating or unsafe cascade. A frontier state
has cost

``` text
normalized goal size + 5 * search level
```

so the fixed level weight is 5. Children are enumerated eagerly and the
search does not perform dynamic per-goal pruning. Expanded states are
limited by `clasetSearch.node_limit`, which defaults to 100000; a
non-positive setting disables the limit.

The theorem list locally accepts `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`,
`SDest`, `Dest` and `Del` markers. Every unmarked theorem is inserted as an
assumption before search starts. Content-bearing generic simplifier
wrappers are unwrapped and inserted; inert generic controls are ignored.

The tactic succeeds only with a replayed proof that closes the goal.

### Failure

Fails when the frontier is exhausted or the node limit is reached without
a complete proof. Malformed marked rules can also cause failure.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem astar_tac_example:
  (p ==> q) /\ (q ==> r) ==> p ==> r
Proof
  classicalLib.ASTAR_TAC []
QED
```

